":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\r\n\r\nClasses in `sqlalchemy.orm.collections` module were renamed in SQLAlchemy 2.0, but some of the legacy names are not imported by `sqlalchemy.orm.collections.*` while the others are.\r\nIt's ideal that the behavior is consistent for all legacy class names.\r\n\r\n### Optional link from https://docs.sqlalchemy.org which documents the behavior that is expected\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### SQLAlchemy Version in Use\r\n\r\n2.0.30\r\n\r\n### DBAPI (i.e. the database driver)\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n### Database Vendor and Major Version\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n### Python Version\r\n\r\n3.11.7\r\n\r\n### Operating system\r\n\r\nFedora 38\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n```\r\n>>> from sqlalchemy.orm.collections import *\r\n>>> attribute_mapped_collection\r\n>>> MappedCollection\r\n```\r\n\r\nMappedCollection and attribute_mapped_collection are both legacy names but only attribute_mapped_collection is not loaded.\r\n\r\n### Error\r\n\r\n```\r\n>>> from sqlalchemy.orm.collections import *\r\n>>> attribute_mapped_collection\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\nNameError: name 'attribute_mapped_collection' is not defined\r\n>>> MappedCollection\r\n<class 'sqlalchemy.orm.mapped_collection.KeyFuncDict'> \r\n```\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https